#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:2
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr "Fehlerbehebung"

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:6
msgid "Command Line"
msgstr "Befehlszeile"

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:8
msgid ""
"The command line interface is the most basic (though not the most "
"convenient) way to troubleshoot PartCAD configuration, model declarations"
" and definitions."
msgstr ""
"Die Befehlszeilenschnittstelle ist die grundlegendste (wenn auch nicht "
"die bequemste) Möglichkeit, Fehler in der PartCAD-Konfiguration, den "
"Modelldeklarationen und -definitionen zu beheben."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:13
msgid "Status"
msgstr "Status"

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:15
msgid ""
"The status of PartCAD context can be evaluated using the ``system "
"status`` command."
msgstr ""
"Der Status des PartCAD-Kontexts kann mit dem Befehl ``system status`` "
"ausgewertet werden."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:21
msgid ""
"Pay attention to any exception or error message produced by the "
"``status`` command."
msgstr ""
"Achten Sie auf jede Ausnahme- oder Fehlermeldung, die der Befehl "
"``status`` ausgibt."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:24
msgid ""
"The same command has two more reports, for the two things that most often"
" turn out to be the answer -- what the configuration actually resolved "
"to, and what the environment actually said:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:33
msgid ""
"They are worth reading together. The first says what an option resolved "
"to once the configuration file, the ``PC_*`` environment and the command "
"line had all been applied; the second says what the environment asked "
"for. They disagree whenever a command-line option won, a variable was "
"misspelled, or a value was rejected -- which covers most of the cases "
"where somebody runs either of them. Variables whose names say they carry "
"a credential are listed but printed as ``<scrubbed>``, so the output is "
"something you can attach to a bug report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:41
msgid ""
"If the work is being done by a daemon -- which it is for most commands --"
" ask the daemon the same two questions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:50
msgid ""
"A daemon is warm and shared per workspace, so the configuration and "
"environment it reports are whatever its own environment held when "
"something first started it, possibly days ago and possibly from a VS Code"
" window. Your command does not run under them -- every command hands the "
"daemon its own resolved configuration -- but the daemon's own copy is "
"what it falls back on, and the environment it inherited is not something "
"this side can reconstruct any other way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:58
msgid "Health Check"
msgstr "Health Check"

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:60
msgid ""
"The ``healthcheck`` command can also be used to verify if the PartCAD "
"environment on your workstation is setup correctly."
msgstr ""
"Mit dem Befehl ``healthcheck`` lässt sich außerdem prüfen, ob die "
"PartCAD-Umgebung auf Ihrer Arbeitsstation korrekt eingerichtet ist."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:67
msgid ""
"Please, follow the instructions provided by the ``healthcheck`` command "
"to fix any issues it detects."
msgstr ""
"Bitte folgen Sie den Anweisungen des Befehls ``healthcheck``, um alle "
"erkannten Probleme zu beheben."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:70
msgid "Use ``--dry-run`` option to see what healthcheck tests can be executed."
msgstr ""
"Verwenden Sie die Option ``--dry-run``, um zu sehen, welche Healthcheck-"
"Tests ausgeführt werden können."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:76
msgid ""
"The ``healthcheck`` command also can take a ``--fix`` option to "
"automatically fix the issues it detects if possible."
msgstr ""
"Der Befehl ``healthcheck`` kann außerdem die Option ``--fix`` "
"entgegennehmen, um erkannte Probleme nach Möglichkeit automatisch zu "
"beheben."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:83
msgid ""
"In order to selectively execute only a subset of the healthchecks tests, "
"the ``healthcheck`` command can be used with the ``--filters`` option "
"that accepts a comma-separated list of test tags."
msgstr ""
"Um gezielt nur eine Teilmenge der Healthcheck-Tests auszuführen, kann der"
" Befehl ``healthcheck`` mit der Option ``--filters`` verwendet werden, "
"die eine durch Kommas getrennte Liste von Test-Tags akzeptiert."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:89
msgid ""
"Most of what ``healthcheck`` finds is reported as a warning and the "
"command still succeeds, because most of it is a machine missing something"
" it can do without. There is one exception, and it is about sandboxes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:94
msgid "Can this machine render anything?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:96
msgid ""
"PartCAD imports no CAD kernel of its own. Every part is produced by a "
"script run in a sandbox, and there are two mechanisms that can provide "
"one on a machine that starts with nothing: conda, which installs an "
"interpreter and the CAD stack beside it, and a container runtime, which "
"carries both already. Three checks report on this, and they share the "
"``sandbox`` tag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:106
msgid ""
"``CondaAvailable`` -- a warning when conda or mamba cannot be found. "
"PartCAD builds a virtual environment instead, which works wherever the "
"host has a usable Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:109
msgid ""
"``DockerAvailable`` -- a warning when no container runtime answers. Note "
"that a Docker daemon running *Windows* containers counts as none here: "
"every image PartCAD uses is a Linux image. Set ``useDocker: false`` (or "
"``PC_USE_DOCKER=false``) on a machine that has a daemon and should not "
"use it, and the check stops looking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:114
msgid ""
"``SandboxAvailable`` -- an **error**, and the only check that makes ``pc "
"healthcheck`` exit non-zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:117
msgid ""
"A stated ``pythonSandbox`` is obeyed, and that is most of what "
"``SandboxAvailable`` does. \"Is there conda or a container\" is the right"
" question only when nobody has said which sandbox to use, because that is"
" when PartCAD is the one choosing between them. If you wrote "
"``pythonSandbox: venv`` -- a CI job that builds a virtual environment "
"from the interpreter it already has, an air-gapped machine, a container "
"image with no conda in it -- nothing is misconfigured, and the check "
"passes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:130
msgid ""
"A declared sandbox is then checked against what *it* needs and nothing "
"else: ``conda`` needs a conda, ``docker`` needs a container runtime, and "
"``venv``, ``pypy`` and ``none`` need only the Python PartCAD is running "
"under. (``remote`` needs a reachable ``partcad-service-remote-docker``, "
"which is a network address this check does not ping.) Asking for "
"``conda`` on a machine that has none is a failure -- being unable to do "
"what was asked is not a reason to quietly do something else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:138
msgid ""
"Three things need a container specifically, and say so when they are "
"reached rather than in advance: an implementation whose package declares "
"``container:``, importing a KiCad PCB (``useDockerKicad``), and the "
"``docker`` Python sandbox when it was asked for by name. If ``pc "
"render``, ``pc export`` or ``pc inspect`` reports that no container "
"runtime is available, start Docker or take the other route the message "
"names -- for KiCad that is installing KiCad on this machine and setting "
"``useDockerKicad: false``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:147 ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:185
#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:243
msgid "Typical problems"
msgstr "Typische Probleme"

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:149
msgid ""
"When running `pc ...` commands, getting: \"pc is not a recognized "
"command...\""
msgstr ""
"Beim Ausführen von `pc ...`-Befehlen erscheint: „pc is not a recognized "
"command...“"

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:151
msgid ""
"Make sure that Conda environment is activated in the current terminal, "
"for example by running `conda info`"
msgstr ""
"Stellen Sie sicher, dass die Conda-Umgebung im aktuellen Terminal "
"aktiviert ist, zum Beispiel durch Ausführen von `conda info`"

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:152
msgid ""
"With the :ref:`standalone build <standalone-cli>`, there is no "
"environment to activate: the commands are linked into ``~/.local/bin``, "
"which has to be on ``PATH``. Run ``~/.local/bin/pc version`` to confirm "
"the installation itself is fine, then add the directory to ``PATH``."
msgstr ""
"Mit dem :ref:`eigenständigen Build <standalone-cli>` gibt es keine "
"Umgebung zu aktivieren: Die Befehle werden nach ``~/.local/bin`` "
"verlinkt, welches im ``PATH`` enthalten sein muss. Führen Sie "
"``~/.local/bin/pc version`` aus, um zu bestätigen, dass die Installation "
"selbst in Ordnung ist, und fügen Sie das Verzeichnis anschließend zum "
"``PATH`` hinzu."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:156
msgid "Which one is running, the standalone build or a wheel?"
msgstr "Welche Variante läuft, der eigenständige Build oder ein Wheel?"

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:158
msgid ""
"``command -v pc`` says. A path under ``~/.local/share/partcad`` (or "
"wherever ``--install-dir`` pointed) is the standalone build; a path "
"inside a Python environment is the wheel. Having both installed is "
"supported, but only the first on ``PATH`` runs."
msgstr ""
"``command -v pc`` gibt Auskunft. Ein Pfad unter "
"``~/.local/share/partcad`` (oder wo auch immer ``--install-dir`` "
"hingezeigt hat) ist der eigenständige Build; ein Pfad innerhalb einer "
"Python-Umgebung ist das Wheel. Beide gleichzeitig installiert zu haben "
"wird unterstützt, aber es läuft nur das, was im ``PATH`` zuerst gefunden "
"wird."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:162
msgid "Imports hang, or time out reaching a repository the browser can open:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:164
msgid ""
"The network is very likely one where a proxy is the only route out. "
"PartCAD reads ``HTTPS_PROXY``, ``HTTP_PROXY`` and ``NO_PROXY`` for "
"everything it downloads -- git repositories, tarballs and ``fileFrom: "
"url`` files alike -- so exporting them is usually the whole fix. See :ref"
":`proxy-configuration`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:168
msgid ""
"If a fetch fails to verify a certificate rather than hanging, the proxy "
"is re-terminating TLS and its CA is not trusted here. Point "
"``SSL_CERT_FILE`` and ``REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE`` at the proxy's CA bundle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:173
msgid "PartCAD VSCode Extension"
msgstr "PartCAD-VSCode-Erweiterung"

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:175
msgid ""
"The recommended way to use PartCAD is by using the Visual Studio "
"Extension called ``PartCAD``. Follow the extension documentation for "
"instructions on how to use this extension."
msgstr ""
"Der empfohlene Weg, PartCAD zu nutzen, ist die Verwendung der Visual-"
"Studio-Code-Erweiterung namens ``PartCAD``. Folgen Sie der "
"Erweiterungsdokumentation für Anweisungen zur Nutzung dieser Erweiterung."

#: ../../source/troubleshooting.rst:179
msgid ""
"For troubleshooting purposes, the ``PartCAD`` terminal view output may "
"not suffice due to the ephemeral nature of some output in that view (many"
" output lines get overwritten). To get the complete and detailed error "
"log, see the ``PartCAD`` output in the ``Output`` view."
msgstr ""
"Zur Fehlerbehebung reicht die Ausgabe der ``PartCAD``-Terminalansicht "
"möglicherweise nicht aus, da einige Ausgaben in dieser Ansicht flüchtig "
"sind (viele Ausgabezeilen werden überschrieben). Das vollständige und "
"detaillierte Fehlerprotokoll finden Sie in der ``PartCAD``-Ausgabe in der"
" ``Output``-Ansicht."

